263
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,095
- [Crow] Did I get
anything on my butt?

264
00:09:22,128 --> 00:09:24,732
- I'm still trembling, I guess.

265
00:09:25,967 --> 00:09:27,502
What's the matter?

266
00:09:27,535 --> 00:09:29,503
Why do you sit and stare
at me like that?

267
00:09:29,537 --> 00:09:31,138
- [Tom] Well, huh, huh,
you know it.

268
00:09:31,172 --> 00:09:32,740
- I don't know, so few
women come this way.

269
00:09:32,773 --> 00:09:34,675
- [Joel] With so few clothes.

270
00:09:34,708 --> 00:09:35,710
- And so?

271
00:09:35,743 --> 00:09:38,145
- As long as you're here,
I might as well.

272
00:09:38,178 --> 00:09:40,580
I never saw a girl
more beautiful.

273
00:09:40,615 --> 00:09:41,415
- Oh.

274
00:09:41,448 --> 00:09:42,248
- [Tom] Sweet talker.

275
00:09:42,283 --> 00:09:43,117
- [Hercules] I've
come a long way.

276
00:09:43,150 --> 00:09:44,185
Seeing you is worth it.

277
00:09:44,218 --> 00:09:45,518
- How simple men are.

278
00:09:45,552 --> 00:09:46,453
- [Crow] Tell him sister.

279
00:09:46,487 --> 00:09:48,288
- As though I were a
plant or an animal.

280
00:09:48,322 --> 00:09:49,223
- [Tom] Can I water you?

281
00:09:49,257 --> 00:09:51,792
- Still, I thank you, you know.

282
00:09:51,825 --> 00:09:53,393
- [Joel] Oh, looks like
an early Bay Watch.

283
00:09:53,427 --> 00:09:55,630
- I'm telling you the truth,
don't thank me for it.

284
00:09:55,663 --> 00:09:58,532
- [Crow] Thank my
personal trainer.

285
00:09:59,633 --> 00:10:01,835
- [Tom] So, uh, wanna look
for agates or something?

286
00:10:01,868 --> 00:10:04,072
- You couldn't be anyone
but Hercules the Theban.

287
00:10:04,105 --> 00:10:06,473
- [Crow] Thank you.

288
00:10:06,507 --> 00:10:08,275
- I know you're expected.

289
00:10:08,308 --> 00:10:09,943
Everything will change,
they say.

290
00:10:09,977 --> 00:10:12,112
- I, (sniffing)

291
00:10:12,145 --> 00:10:15,448
- [Tom] Holy cow I'm hungry,
I gotta go.

292
00:10:18,752 --> 00:10:20,888
- [Hercules] By the gods,
everything's burnt by this time.

293
00:10:20,922 --> 00:10:22,690
- [Crow] Still, Lassie
will taste good right now.

294
00:10:22,723 --> 00:10:23,857
- [Joel] Ew.

295
00:10:23,890 --> 00:10:24,692
- [Crow] Sit, stay.

296
00:10:24,725 --> 00:10:25,660
- No, well done, perhaps.

297
00:10:25,693 --> 00:10:28,128
- [Tom] Here, want some meat?

298
00:10:29,997 --> 00:10:31,365
No Pace picante sauce?

299
00:10:31,398 --> 00:10:32,265
Get the rope.

300
00:10:32,298 --> 00:10:33,233
- Will you have a piece?

301
00:10:33,267 --> 00:10:34,335
- [Crow] Of that?

302
00:10:34,368 --> 00:10:35,937
- Go on.

303
00:10:35,970 --> 00:10:38,472
- [Tom] Come on, taste it all.

304
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,577
- [Crow] Yech, this is
really weird, Herc.

305
00:10:42,610 --> 00:10:43,610
- Go on.

306
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:45,078
- No more, thank you.

307
00:10:45,112 --> 00:10:46,147
- [Joel] I'm on Jenny Craig.

308
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:48,248
- I will start where
your lips have touched.

309
00:10:48,282 --> 00:10:50,250
- Why how dare you be
so audacious?

310
00:10:50,283 --> 00:10:51,552
- I'm too hungry to help it.

311
00:10:51,585 --> 00:10:52,687
- [Crow] It's my piece o' meat,

312
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:53,787
I'll bite it where I want to.

313
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:56,157
(sloppy lipsmacking)

314
00:10:56,190 --> 00:10:57,057
- [Tom] Hey, long as
you're over there,

315
00:10:57,090 --> 00:11:00,560
hook me a Primo outta the
fridge, will ya?

316
00:11:02,162 --> 00:11:03,230
- [Joel] Pig.

317
00:11:04,565 --> 00:11:05,498
- [Tom] Thor, hey buddy.

318
00:11:05,532 --> 00:11:08,768
- [Crow] Oh, wouldn't you know,
a flat.

319
00:11:09,703 --> 00:11:12,540
- [Tom] Hey, you
gotta box wrench?

320
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:16,443
- That is no work
for a princess.

321
00:11:16,477 --> 00:11:20,047
Yes, you are Iole, daughter
of Pelias, king of Julco.

322
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:22,248
The royal standard on the
chariot told me your name.

323
00:11:22,282 --> 00:11:23,850
- [Joel] I used to lift
with your brother.

324
00:11:23,883 --> 00:11:25,318
- Here, let me do it.

325
00:11:25,352 --> 00:11:27,187
I can work much faster.

326
00:11:27,220 --> 00:11:28,955
- There's lots of time.

327
00:11:28,988 --> 00:11:30,925
To return to a city
that I hate so.

328
00:11:30,958 --> 00:11:32,158
- [Crow] Detroit?

329
00:11:32,192 --> 00:11:35,028
- That's no way to
welcome a stranger.

330
00:11:35,062 --> 00:11:36,930
- Only you've no
right to be here.

331
00:11:36,963 --> 00:11:38,532
- Your father knows about it.

332
00:11:38,565 --> 00:11:39,900
- He didn't ask you.

333
00:11:39,933 --> 00:11:42,035
It was a question of teaching
the art of war to a fetus,

334
00:11:42,068 --> 00:11:42,903
my brother, and you offered to.

335
00:11:42,937 --> 00:11:43,770
- [Joel] A fetus?

336
00:11:43,803 --> 00:11:45,038
- Isn't that the same thing?

337
00:11:45,072 --> 00:11:48,142
- No, you know the
story of my family.

338
00:11:48,175 --> 00:11:50,077
A man named Brady

339
00:11:50,110 --> 00:11:51,478
- Somebody spoke to
you about us.

340
00:11:51,512 --> 00:11:55,315
- [Joel] Did Jean tell
you I liked you?

341
00:11:55,348 --> 00:11:57,083
- You remember it well, then.

342
00:11:57,117 --> 00:11:58,952
Ah yes, I remember it well

343
00:11:58,985 --> 00:12:01,088
- Was it really so bad?

344
00:12:01,122 --> 00:12:04,258
- [Crow] Excuse me while I
have a strange interlude.

345
00:12:04,292 --> 00:12:05,658
- I remember it now.

346
00:12:05,692 --> 00:12:06,560
- [Tom] Uh oh.

347
00:12:06,593 --> 00:12:08,762
I remember all that went on.

348
00:12:08,795 --> 00:12:10,230
- [Joel] (heavy sign) Oh boy.

349
00:12:10,263 --> 00:12:12,332
- Is it wrong to be as
happy as I was then?

350
00:12:12,365 --> 00:12:13,833
But the gods won't answer
that question.

351
00:12:13,867 --> 00:12:15,635
- [Crow] It's a simple yes
or no woulda been fine.

352
00:12:15,668 --> 00:12:17,872
- They turn from me when I ask.

353
00:12:17,905 --> 00:12:20,407
I was only a child that day,
10 years ago.

354
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,775
- [Crow] Previously,
on Hercules.

355
00:12:21,808 --> 00:12:23,577
- [Iole] It had been such
a happy afternoon for me.

356
00:12:23,610 --> 00:12:26,280
We were returning from the
hunt with my Uncle Aeson,

357
00:12:26,313 --> 00:12:28,182
who was king of Julco
at that time.

358
00:12:28,215 --> 00:12:31,385
He insisted that his son
Jason ride in his chariot,

359
00:12:31,418 --> 00:12:35,655
together with my brother
Iphitos, my father and I.

360
00:12:35,688 --> 00:12:38,292
- [Tom] And the horses,
don't forget us.

361
00:12:38,325 --> 00:12:42,228
- [Iole] At our side rode the
captain of the escort, Chiron,

362
00:12:42,262 --> 00:12:44,498
who had had angry words with
the king on the previous day.

363
00:12:44,532 --> 00:12:45,565
- [Crow] I'm angry.

364
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:47,400
- [Iole] And we did not
know what it was about.

365
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:49,303
(horse hooves clopping)

366
00:12:49,337 --> 00:12:51,205
In the woods,
- Guard, halt.

367
00:12:51,238 --> 00:12:52,038
Left face.

368
00:12:52,072 --> 00:12:52,740
- [Iole] We suddenly
saw a platoon

369
00:12:52,773 --> 00:12:53,873
of soldiers coming toward us.

370
00:12:53,907 --> 00:12:55,442
- [Tom] Hey, I found a pack
of Trojans in the road.

371
00:12:55,475 --> 00:12:56,343
- [Iole] There was a
man in chains.

372
00:12:56,377 --> 00:12:59,078
- [Joel] (laughing)
That's disgusting.

373
00:12:59,112 --> 00:13:00,647
- [Crow] Look what you did, bad.

374
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:03,017
- [Iole] My uncle
stopped the chariot.

375
00:13:03,050 --> 00:13:05,618
I tried to see the face
of the prisoner,

376
00:13:05,652 --> 00:13:08,255
but he knelt with his
head bent very low.

377
00:13:08,288 --> 00:13:10,892
The king whispered something
in my father's ear.

378
00:13:10,925 --> 00:13:12,993
As my father got down
from the chariot

379
00:13:13,027 --> 00:13:14,962
and went to talk with the
officer of the platoon.

380
00:13:14,995 --> 00:13:15,897
- [Joel] Ah, but first he
pulled his skirt

381
00:13:15,930 --> 00:13:18,165
out of his underpants.

382
00:13:18,198 --> 00:13:20,500
- What is he charged with?

383
00:13:20,533 --> 00:13:21,468
- [Tom] Blocking the road.

384
00:13:21,502 --> 00:13:22,468
- [Guard] He killed a
woman and robbed her

385
00:13:22,503 --> 00:13:24,305
of what little money she
had, your Excellency.

386
00:13:24,338 --> 00:13:25,772
- [Joel] Oh oui, I
did that thing.

387
00:13:25,805 --> 00:13:29,108
- [Tom] Hmm, wrap him up,
I'll take him.

388
00:13:29,142 --> 00:13:30,677
- You like to kill, ay?

389
00:13:30,710 --> 00:13:32,378
- [Iole] To kill, that
was the only word

390
00:13:32,412 --> 00:13:34,448
I was able to understand
of the brief conversation

391
00:13:34,482 --> 00:13:36,250
that followed.

392
00:13:36,283 --> 00:13:39,920
But I knew somehow that the
man must be condemned to death.

393
00:13:39,953 --> 00:13:41,555
- [Crow] It's a murderer,
nothin' to worry about.

394
00:13:41,588 --> 00:13:43,423
- [Iole] My father came
back to the chariot,

395
00:13:43,457 --> 00:13:44,892
and whispered
something to my uncle.

396
00:13:44,925 --> 00:13:48,395
- [Tom] Excuse me, are
you Hector Elizondo?

397
00:13:48,428 --> 00:13:50,163
- [Iole] The king shook his
head and we started off again.

398
00:13:50,197 --> 00:13:53,367
(goofy twang singing)

399
00:13:59,138 --> 00:14:00,407
- The thought of person as dead

400
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:02,408
swept over me like a bad omen.

401
00:14:02,442 --> 00:14:05,245
- [Crow] Three, the
final conflict.

402
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:11,485
- [Tom] Dark and stormy night.

403
00:14:11,552 --> 00:14:15,055
- [Iole] Later on, my sleep
was filled with nightmares.

404
00:14:15,088 --> 00:14:18,392
The memory of what happened in
the woods would not leave me.

405
00:14:18,458 --> 00:14:20,360
Again and again, I pictured
what would certainly

406
00:14:20,393 --> 00:14:21,762
be the end of that
terrible storm.

407
00:14:21,795 --> 00:14:23,663
- [Crow] Yeah, never
eat Mexican at bedtime.

408
00:14:23,697 --> 00:14:24,498
- [Iole] The
condemned man brought

409
00:14:24,532 --> 00:14:26,200
to the place of execution.

410
00:14:26,233 --> 00:14:27,968
The executioner
advancing to him.

411
00:14:28,002 --> 00:14:29,237
Grasping his ax.

412
00:14:29,270 --> 00:14:30,303
- [Tom] Breakfast.

413
00:14:30,337 --> 00:14:31,338
- [Iole] Lifting the ax
and me powerless to help.

414
00:14:31,372 --> 00:14:32,272
(screaming)

415
00:14:32,305 --> 00:14:33,940
- [Joel] I dreamed I
kissed Gavin McLeod.

416
00:14:33,973 --> 00:14:35,042
- [Iole] I heard the scream.

417
00:14:35,075 --> 00:14:35,943
I heard other screams echoing

418
00:14:35,977 --> 00:14:38,045
from the farthest end
of the pass.

419
00:14:38,078 --> 00:14:40,915
(muffled wailing)

420
00:14:41,882 --> 00:14:43,283
My terror was even greater

421
00:14:43,317 --> 00:14:45,518
when I noticed that my
nurses' bed was empty.

422
00:14:45,552 --> 00:14:46,853
- [Tom] Yeah, there was
a real servant problem

423
00:14:46,887 --> 00:14:48,388
in ancient Greece.

424
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:53,793
- [Crow] I decided to put
on some socks.

425
00:14:53,827 --> 00:14:55,662
My feet were freezing.

426
00:14:56,930 --> 00:14:58,065
- [Iole] I was out of my
mind with fear.

427
00:14:58,098 --> 00:14:59,900
I ran to the throne room.

428
00:14:59,933 --> 00:15:01,602
- [Tom] It's a going out
of business sale.

429
00:15:01,635 --> 00:15:06,240
We've lost our empire and
everything is priced to move.

430
00:15:06,273 --> 00:15:07,908
- [Iole] I could scarcely
see the body of the king

431
00:15:07,942 --> 00:15:10,377
as they carried him out amidst
the clamor and confusion.

432
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:12,312
- [Tom] Oh boy.

433
00:15:12,345 --> 00:15:14,080
- [Iole] My father stood there,
petrified.

434
00:15:14,113 --> 00:15:15,315
- [Joel] Oh, who bled here?

435
00:15:15,348 --> 00:15:17,818
Get me some club soda.

436
00:15:17,852 --> 00:15:20,820
- [Iole] Then he turned and a
look of fear crossed his face.

437
00:15:20,853 --> 00:15:23,190
For the stand behind the
throne was empty.

438
00:15:23,223 --> 00:15:24,525
- [Tom] Looks like a Jim
Dine sculpture.

439
00:15:24,558 --> 00:15:27,227
- [Iole] The Golden
Fleece was gone.

440
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:30,397
- [Joel] But I digress,
how was your day?

441
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:32,332
- Jason escaped with the
Golden Fleece.

442
00:15:32,365 --> 00:15:33,200
(snoring)

443
00:15:33,233 --> 00:15:34,435
And Chiron, too, but you
know the rest.

444
00:15:34,468 --> 00:15:37,003
- So that's why Chiron was
accused of killing the king,

445
00:15:37,037 --> 00:15:39,272
kidnapping Jason and
stealing the Golden Fleece.

446
00:15:39,307 --> 00:15:40,407
- Yes.

447
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,308
- And for what reason?

448
00:15:41,342 --> 00:15:43,077
- [Iole] For revenge.

449
00:15:43,110 --> 00:15:44,478
- And you believe that?

450
00:15:44,512 --> 00:15:45,712
- It's important.

451
00:15:45,745 --> 00:15:47,013
Do you think that people lie?

452
00:15:47,047 --> 00:15:47,848
- [Tom] No, never.

453
00:15:47,882 --> 00:15:49,048
Yes, always.

454
00:15:49,082 --> 00:15:51,018
- Well, I've heard it wasn't
Chiron who killed the king.

455
00:15:51,052 --> 00:15:52,720
It was the king's
brother who murdered him.

456
00:15:52,753 --> 00:15:54,655
- That's not true.

457
00:15:54,688 --> 00:15:58,792
- Why do you relive the
story if it's not true?

458
00:15:58,825 --> 00:16:00,793
- [Crow] Hey, my turd
bag's full over here.

459
00:16:00,827 --> 00:16:02,528
Can ya empty this thing?

460
00:16:02,562 --> 00:16:04,898
- They all speak about
the past here.

461
00:16:04,932 --> 00:16:06,200
The murder happened to
put my father

462
00:16:06,233 --> 00:16:08,002
on his brother's throne.

463
00:16:08,035 --> 00:16:10,770
But I know he wouldn't do that.

464
00:16:10,803 --> 00:16:12,272
Tragic.

465
00:16:12,305 --> 00:16:14,442
Now that the Golden Fleece
is gone, he must officiate.

466
00:16:14,475 --> 00:16:15,608
- [All] Ew.

467
00:16:15,642 --> 00:16:18,378
- But when you try to aid
them, why they don't care.

468
00:16:18,412 --> 00:16:20,780
My poor father's above
your suspicions.

469
00:16:20,813 --> 00:16:22,348
- For all our sakes, I hope so.

470
00:16:22,382 --> 00:16:24,017
- [Joel] Anyway, this should
hold 'til you get to Sparta.

471
00:16:24,050 --> 00:16:24,785
- I see you're joking.

472
00:16:24,818 --> 00:16:25,952
- [All] Ah, ha, ha, ha.

473
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:30,490
- I remember somebody saying
you're a friend of Chiron.

474
00:16:30,523 --> 00:16:32,458
Have you come for revenge?

475
00:16:32,492 --> 00:16:34,528
And more suffering?

476
00:16:34,562 --> 00:16:37,063
- Wait, would you allow
me to accompany you?

477
00:16:37,097 --> 00:16:37,898
- [Tom] On piano?

478
00:16:37,932 --> 00:16:38,732
- Please.

479
00:16:38,765 --> 00:16:40,167
- [Crow] Let's start the movie.

480
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:41,468
- I'm not much of a carpenter.

481
00:16:41,502 --> 00:16:42,737
It won't work.

482
00:16:42,770 --> 00:16:45,338
It's better to let me
take you back to Julco.

483
00:16:45,372 --> 00:16:46,940
- [Tom] There's a new
Sophocles play opening tonight.

484
00:16:46,973 --> 00:16:48,575
- Come with me, please?

485
00:16:48,608 --> 00:16:51,812
- [Crow] Pretty please,
with Herc on top?

486
00:16:51,845 --> 00:16:53,880
- I would like to see your eyes

487
00:16:53,913 --> 00:16:55,815
with happiness there in
place of hate.

488
00:16:55,848 --> 00:16:58,585
Because I can understand
just the way you feel,

489
00:16:58,618 --> 00:17:00,087
but I will help you now.

490
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:01,655
Believe me.

491
00:17:01,688 --> 00:17:03,123
I'll protect you.

492
00:17:05,258 --> 00:17:07,160
- [Joel] Um, Hercules,
tell me again.

493
00:17:07,193 --> 00:17:09,763
Why didn't we take the chariot?

494
00:17:11,432 --> 00:17:15,002
- [Crow] Can we stop
at a SuperAmerica soon?

495
00:17:15,035 --> 00:17:17,437
- [Tom] It's okay, just hush.

496
00:17:22,008 --> 00:17:25,245
Hercules now concludes
his broadcasting day.

497
00:17:25,278 --> 00:17:27,848
Good night, and may Herc bless.

498
00:17:30,083 --> 00:17:32,753
(dramatic music)

499
00:17:32,787 --> 00:17:35,888
- [Crow] Where is the sample?

500
00:17:35,922 --> 00:17:39,025
- [Joel] Oops, boy I'd hate to
shovel those steps, ya know?

501
00:17:39,058 --> 00:17:39,893
Just whoa.

502
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:43,563
- [Tom] Hi, Hercules,
reservation for two.

503
00:17:43,597 --> 00:17:46,433
It might be under
Heracles though.

504
00:17:47,935 --> 00:17:49,537
- [Joel] Oh, no, really,
they take this cheese,

505
00:17:49,570 --> 00:17:51,605
they get it really hot,
and then they pour retsina

506
00:17:51,638 --> 00:17:54,742
all over the top, and then they
light it and they say, opa.

507
00:17:54,775 --> 00:17:56,743
- As the worm eats the
fruit that matures.

508
00:17:56,777 --> 00:17:57,878
- [All] Ew.

509
00:17:57,912 --> 00:18:01,715
- As men stalk their prey,
he will come here for you.

510
00:18:01,748 --> 00:18:03,817
When you see the man,
he will wear one sandal.

511
00:18:03,850 --> 00:18:05,118
Wait no longer.

512
00:18:05,152 --> 00:18:07,453
- [Crow] She has a
creamy strawberry center.

513
00:18:07,487 --> 00:18:10,057
- Will you escape destruction?

514
00:18:10,090 --> 00:18:12,492
He wears but a single sandal.

515
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:14,762
When he comes, take care.

516
00:18:14,795 --> 00:18:16,230
- But why does he hate
me like that?

517
00:18:16,263 --> 00:18:18,498
- He does not know you
are the man he hates.

518
00:18:18,532 --> 00:18:20,100
- Oh, father,

519
00:18:20,133 --> 00:18:21,802
how can you take stock in
these oracles?

520
00:18:21,835 --> 00:18:23,270
And this one isn't even pretty.

521
00:18:23,303 --> 00:18:25,705
- Destiny knows about all men,
and when you're time comes,

522
00:18:25,738 --> 00:18:26,840
you too will know.

523
00:18:26,873 --> 00:18:28,842
- You witch, get away,
do you hear?

524
00:18:28,875 --> 00:18:30,543
- They will speak no more.

525
00:18:30,577 --> 00:18:32,947
When someone angers the gods,
they finish.

526
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:33,513
- Why--

527
00:18:33,547 --> 00:18:34,413
- No.

528
00:18:34,447 --> 00:18:35,448
- [Tom] Can we not fight
just this once?

529
00:18:35,482 --> 00:18:36,917
- Iphitus, respect the
gods and their oracles.

530
00:18:36,950 --> 00:18:38,185
They are the gods messengers.

531
00:18:38,218 --> 00:18:39,653
- [Crow] Just askin'
about the oracle.

532
00:18:39,687 --> 00:18:41,588
- I shall give an order
that any man coming to Julco

533
00:18:41,622 --> 00:18:44,057
(chattering)

534
00:18:46,427 --> 00:18:47,293
You.

535
00:18:47,327 --> 00:18:48,395
- [Crow] How long have
you been there?

536
00:18:48,428 --> 00:18:49,830
- Who is that?

537
00:18:49,863 --> 00:18:52,867
- Hercules, the master of
arms that you sent for.

538
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:53,967
- Hercules the Theban.

539
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,303
- [Joel] Hey, I'm no Thebe.

540
00:18:57,370 --> 00:18:58,172
- [Pelias] Come forward.

541
00:18:58,205 --> 00:18:59,873
- [Crow] May I take
your luggage?

542
00:18:59,907 --> 00:19:01,542
- [Joel] You're next.

543
00:19:01,575 --> 00:19:05,645
(mysterious warbling tone)

544
00:19:05,678 --> 00:19:06,747
- Welcome to Julco.

545
00:19:06,780 --> 00:19:07,813
- [Tom] A planned community.

546
00:19:07,848 --> 00:19:09,182
- They say you're almost a god.

547
00:19:09,215 --> 00:19:10,650
Well then, why aren't
you invisible?

548
00:19:10,683 --> 00:19:11,918
- Stop it Iphitus.

549
00:19:11,952 --> 00:19:13,553
This man saved my life today.

550
00:19:13,587 --> 00:19:15,522
- Marvelous, that's a way
to make a fine impression.

551
00:19:15,555 --> 00:19:17,925
- You better listen to what
I have to say to Hercules,

552
00:19:17,958 --> 00:19:20,227
because it concerns you, too.

553
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:21,928
You're here to reinforce Julco.

554
00:19:21,962 --> 00:19:22,462
- [Crow] Done.

555
00:19:22,495 --> 00:19:23,597
And?

556
00:19:23,630 --> 00:19:25,898
- Hercules will guide you
until you're able to reign.

557
00:19:25,932 --> 00:19:27,935
But I, he must show you.

558
00:19:29,302 --> 00:19:30,870
Because I want to give
the throne up.

559
00:19:30,903 --> 00:19:31,638
- Father.

560
00:19:31,672 --> 00:19:32,572
- [Crow] Princess, please.

561
00:19:32,605 --> 00:19:35,042
- Because each year I
grow more anxious.

562
00:19:35,075 --> 00:19:37,677
I can't go on being
king forever.

563
00:19:37,710 --> 00:19:38,612
I can't go on.

564
00:19:38,645 --> 00:19:39,680
- [Tom] I'll go on.

565
00:19:39,713 --> 00:19:41,815
- Father, you've been
drinking too much tonight.

566
00:19:41,848 --> 00:19:43,417
- I guess you're right,
but it won't stop it,

567
00:19:43,450 --> 00:19:44,383
can't you see?

568
00:19:44,417 --> 00:19:45,752
(burping)

569
00:19:45,785 --> 00:19:47,988
Hercules, I must beg
you to help us at Julco.

570
00:19:48,022 --> 00:19:49,757
- [Crow] Just said you were
drinkin' too much, geez.

571
00:19:49,790 --> 00:19:53,360
- You must help to keep
the throne for my boy here.

572
00:19:53,393 --> 00:19:54,995
If I find that you are loyal,

573
00:19:55,062 --> 00:19:57,797
I will grant you anything
you want out of Julco.

574
00:19:57,863 --> 00:19:58,698
- [Tom] Anything?

575
00:19:58,765 --> 00:19:59,767
- I hope you will sleep well.

576
00:19:59,800 --> 00:20:01,968
(snuffling)

577
00:20:02,970 --> 00:20:05,972
One moment, he may be an
imposter, how do I know?

578
00:20:06,005 --> 00:20:07,173
- [Joel] Have another drink,
dad.

579
00:20:07,207 --> 00:20:08,275
- But I saw him.

580
00:20:08,308 --> 00:20:10,243
My horses, they were
running away.

581
00:20:10,277 --> 00:20:11,745
- [Crow] Here, benchpress me.

582
00:20:11,778 --> 00:20:13,113
- He stopped my horses.

583
00:20:13,147 --> 00:20:14,113
I knew who he was.

584
00:20:14,147 --> 00:20:14,982
- Certainly.

585
00:20:15,015 --> 00:20:15,948
- [Joel] Why, he could
be Roy Rogers.

586
00:20:15,982 --> 00:20:17,750
- And I'm truly grateful.

587
00:20:17,783 --> 00:20:20,053
But I can't depend on the
eyes of a girl.

588
00:20:20,087 --> 00:20:21,455
- What are you trying to say?

589
00:20:21,488 --> 00:20:23,190
- [Tom] I'm a pig.

590
00:20:23,223 --> 00:20:24,323
- Nothing.

591
00:20:24,357 --> 00:20:25,958
Don't be upset about it, Iole.

592
00:20:25,992 --> 00:20:27,627
- [Crow] Why don't we talk
about it later.

593
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:31,097
- Well then, let me
do it father.

594
00:20:31,130 --> 00:20:33,233
- [Joel] You a billiards man,
Herc?

595
00:20:33,267 --> 00:20:35,202
- Alright then, prove
yourself fearless.

596
00:20:35,235 --> 00:20:36,068
Come on.

597
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:41,842
- [Crow] What are you doin'?

598
00:20:41,875 --> 00:20:43,610
That's my good spear.

599
00:20:45,578 --> 00:20:47,780
(grunting and groaning)

600
00:20:47,813 --> 00:20:49,683
- [Tom] I'll bend it back later.

601
00:20:49,717 --> 00:20:50,517
(metal clanging)

602
00:20:50,550 --> 00:20:51,352
- Good, Hercules.

603
00:20:51,385 --> 00:20:52,185
- [Crow] Sit, Hercules.

604
00:20:52,218 --> 00:20:53,020
- Enough now.

605
00:20:53,053 --> 00:20:55,388
Iole may show you to
your quarters.

606
00:20:55,422 --> 00:20:56,790
- Until tomorrow, Pelias.

607
00:20:56,823 --> 00:20:58,958
- [Joel] Well here's where
the workin' out pays off.

608
00:20:58,992 --> 00:21:00,660
- Why do you have to treat
me as if I were a baby?

609
00:21:00,693 --> 00:21:01,695
(sniveling and mewling)

610
00:21:01,728 --> 00:21:03,630
He's taken you in, just
as he's charmed Iole.

611
00:21:03,663 --> 00:21:05,165
- And you have him because
you're weak and impulsive.

612
00:21:05,198 --> 00:21:06,065
- [Tom] I'm not.

613
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:06,933
Am I?

614
00:21:06,967 --> 00:21:08,502
- Hercules is a guarantee.

615
00:21:08,535 --> 00:21:10,403
He's more than a match
to play against Argos,

616
00:21:10,437 --> 00:21:12,372
Laertes, Tifi, Dijustria,
and all those others

617
00:21:12,405 --> 00:21:15,542
who plan to get the
throne of Julco.

618
00:21:15,575 --> 00:21:17,343
I want that throne for you.

619
00:21:17,377 --> 00:21:19,880
- [Crow] Ooh, I want
that throne.

620
00:21:19,913 --> 00:21:21,715
(steam hissing)
(door slamming)

621
00:21:21,748 --> 00:21:23,117
(crackling)
(swishing)

622
00:21:23,150 --> 00:21:26,285
(rolling)
(door closing)

623
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:29,188
(clamping)
(slamming)

624
00:21:29,222 --> 00:21:30,357
(hissing)

625
00:21:30,390 --> 00:21:33,227
- Joel, what was the deal
with the ancient Greeks, huh?

626
00:21:33,260 --> 00:21:34,527
- Hey be careful, you're talkin'
about

627
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:36,195
the ancient Greeks, Crow.

628
00:21:36,228 --> 00:21:37,563
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

629
00:21:37,597 --> 00:21:40,100
But this constellation jazz,
come on.

630
00:21:40,133 --> 00:21:41,535
After 2000 years, can
we finally admit

631
00:21:41,568 --> 00:21:43,437
the emperor has no clothes?

632
00:21:43,470 --> 00:21:46,105
Four stars, oh, it's
a great pair.

633
00:21:46,138 --> 00:21:48,608
Right, or Cassiopeia,
whatever the heck that is.

634
00:21:48,642 --> 00:21:49,442
- Hey, what about Orion?

635
00:21:49,475 --> 00:21:51,978
- Okay, okay, I'll
give ya Orion.

636
00:21:52,012 --> 00:21:53,413
I gotta admit, Orion's alright,

637
00:21:53,447 --> 00:21:54,613
but the rest of 'em, it
just doesn't--

638
00:21:54,647 --> 00:21:56,750
- (throat clearing) If I
could step in here, please.

639
00:21:56,783 --> 00:21:59,085
Lest we despoil the reputation,
Crow,

640
00:21:59,118 --> 00:22:01,320
of the founders of
democracy too much.

641
00:22:01,355 --> 00:22:04,323
The reason you don't see the
same figures in the night sky

642
00:22:04,357 --> 00:22:06,893
is because new constellations
have never been identified

643
00:22:06,927 --> 00:22:09,328
to reflect modern tastes
and sensibilities.

644
00:22:09,362 --> 00:22:10,163
- You've done that?

645
00:22:10,197 --> 00:22:10,997
- I've done that.

646
00:22:11,030 --> 00:22:11,832
A little help here, Joel?

647
00:22:11,865 --> 00:22:12,998
Uh, watch carefully.

648
00:22:13,033 --> 00:22:16,135
The first grouping of stars
found in the southern sky,

649
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:19,505
forms a constellation for even
the simplest hayseed, Crow.

650
00:22:19,538 --> 00:22:21,375
Yes, it's a ham sammich.

651
00:22:21,408 --> 00:22:23,477
Fascinatingly, the star to
the left of the main group

652
00:22:23,510 --> 00:22:25,178
forms a perfect pickle.

653
00:22:25,212 --> 00:22:26,480
Next.

654
00:22:26,513 --> 00:22:27,847
As winter gives way to spring,

655
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:29,548
the eastern sky is
ablaze with the glory of

656
00:22:29,582 --> 00:22:31,385
the New Christy Minstrels.

657
00:22:31,418 --> 00:22:32,952
- New Christy Minstrels?

658
00:22:32,985 --> 00:22:34,453
Who woulda ever thought that?

659
00:22:34,487 --> 00:22:35,588
- Well, that's why you
need people like me

660
00:22:35,622 --> 00:22:36,757
and the Greeks, Joel, next.

661
00:22:36,790 --> 00:22:37,390
- Oh brother.

662
00:22:37,423 --> 00:22:38,425
- Sophist.

663
00:22:38,458 --> 00:22:40,927
Dodi Siemen just may be
tempted to once again

664
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:42,028
navigate by the stars,

665
00:22:42,062 --> 00:22:43,997
when they recognize in
this group of 11,

666
00:22:44,030 --> 00:22:46,165
Guernica, Picasso's
cubist masterpiece,

667
00:22:46,198 --> 00:22:48,368
portraying the horrors
of the Spanish Civil War.

668
00:22:48,402 --> 00:22:50,737
- Well, talk about your
modern sensibilities.

669
00:22:50,770 --> 00:22:52,472
Really good job, Tom Servo,

670
00:22:52,505 --> 00:22:55,042
for these renovations
of old constellations.

671
00:22:55,075 --> 00:22:57,043
- And I've salvaged the
reputations of the ancient
Greeks.

672
00:22:57,077 --> 00:22:58,043
- Well done.

673
00:22:58,078 --> 00:22:59,913
- Tom, I regret my
earlier sniping

674
00:22:59,947 --> 00:23:03,450
and if you'll allow me, I got
a constellation here, Joel?

675
00:23:03,483 --> 00:23:04,417
- Oh, well that's really n--

676
00:23:04,450 --> 00:23:05,585
- Here, it's a pencil.

677
00:23:05,618 --> 00:23:06,420
- Doh.

678
00:23:06,453 --> 00:23:07,553
- The eraser's almost gone.

679
00:23:07,587 --> 00:23:08,555
- Crow, don't mock me.

680
00:23:08,588 --> 00:23:09,622
You're playin' with fire.

681
00:23:09,655 --> 00:23:11,825
- Hey, two dots, it's a pencil.

682
00:23:11,858 --> 00:23:13,327
What could be more modern?

683
00:23:13,360 --> 00:23:15,895
- I weep for the death of
the spirit and the soul.

684
00:23:15,928 --> 00:23:16,730
- Hey, who doesn't?

685
00:23:16,763 --> 00:23:17,930
We'll be right back.

686
00:23:17,963 --> 00:23:18,798
- En oui

687
00:23:27,507 --> 00:23:30,510
- [Joel] Ah, where's
my Remy Martin?

688
00:23:31,545 --> 00:23:34,647
- [Tom] Friends are
visiting from Europe.

689
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:36,248
(metal clicking)

690
00:23:36,282 --> 00:23:38,185
- [Crow] Uh, you're uh,
drinking my commode.

691
00:23:38,218 --> 00:23:40,187
- It is late for you
to visit here.

692
00:23:40,220 --> 00:23:41,287
What is it Eurysteus?

693
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:43,390
- [Eurysteus] Nothing, but
you have made a mistake.

694
00:23:43,423 --> 00:23:44,223
- [Joel] This is my room.

695
00:23:44,257 --> 00:23:46,425
- No, Hercules will
train Iphitus

696
00:23:46,460 --> 00:23:47,927
to reign here with success.

697
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:48,995
- [Tom] Right here on ESPN.

698
00:23:49,028 --> 00:23:51,498
- [Eurysteus] Hercules
was Chiron's close friend.

699
00:23:51,532 --> 00:23:53,633
He hasn't forgotten
what's happened to him.

700
00:23:53,667 --> 00:23:55,635
- That took place years ago.

701
00:23:55,668 --> 00:23:57,270
- [Eurysteus]
Hercules is honest,

702
00:23:57,303 --> 00:23:59,705
and honesty always
finds the truth,

703
00:23:59,738 --> 00:24:01,340
even after many years.

704
00:24:01,373 --> 00:24:02,408
- [Crow] Is it Dr. No?

705
00:24:02,442 --> 00:24:03,643
- [Eurysteus] His purpose
for coming here is

706
00:24:03,677 --> 00:24:05,145
to clear Chiron's name.

707
00:24:05,178 --> 00:24:06,913
- [Joel] Is it the Millionaire?

708
00:24:06,947 --> 00:24:09,782
- Perhaps he'll find something
else more interesting.

709
00:24:09,817 --> 00:24:11,350
Emotions, for example.

710
00:24:11,383 --> 00:24:12,318
- Iole.

711
00:24:12,352 --> 00:24:13,653
- [Crow] Oh, it's him, that guy,

712
00:24:13,687 --> 00:24:15,322
whoever it is.

713
00:24:15,355 --> 00:24:17,890
- Young people forget
their purposes sometimes.

714
00:24:17,923 --> 00:24:19,458
- [Tom] These kids today,
I tell ya.

715
00:24:19,492 --> 00:24:21,360
- You'll foresee this
man they say, you'll see.

716
00:24:21,393 --> 00:24:22,795
- I know, I know.

717
00:24:24,130 --> 00:24:26,600
- [Joel] Uh, can I
go to bed now?

718
00:24:26,633 --> 00:24:29,435
- I'll be going now, to
my hiding place.

719
00:24:29,468 --> 00:24:32,105
As you promised, it was
the only reward I got.

720
00:24:32,138 --> 00:24:33,038
- [Pelias] And the gold?

721
00:24:33,072 --> 00:24:34,240
- The gold?

722
00:24:34,273 --> 00:24:36,275
But you need light to
see it well.

723
00:24:36,308 --> 00:24:38,077
It's like blood on my hands.

724
00:24:38,110 --> 00:24:38,912
Bloody.

725
00:24:38,945 --> 00:24:39,745
- [Crow] Pussy.

726
00:24:39,778 --> 00:24:40,580
- Like your brother was.

727
00:24:40,613 --> 00:24:41,982
- [Pelias] Get out.

728
00:24:42,015 --> 00:24:44,985
- Very well, because I
can wait 'til you want me.

729
00:24:45,018 --> 00:24:49,455
- [Tom] Because I can
wait 'til you want me.

730
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:51,558
- [Joel] And don't slam
the screen door.

731
00:24:51,592 --> 00:24:52,425
Doh.

732
00:24:56,028 --> 00:25:00,367
- [Crow] It's the Punt,
Pass & Kick competition.

733
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:03,237
- [Tom] It's a Gore
Vidal fantasy.

734
00:25:05,972 --> 00:25:07,107
- [Joel] Would you two
please stop that

735
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:09,877
and get back to training,
please?

736
00:25:10,810 --> 00:25:12,545
- [Crow] I do solemnly swear.

737
00:25:12,578 --> 00:25:13,713
- No more racing, and
I'm not joking,

738
00:25:13,747 --> 00:25:15,515
your heart's strained, you
can't force it.

739
00:25:15,548 --> 00:25:18,150
- I know Aesculapius, but I
want to finish this marathon.

740
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:19,318
- Better take him away.

741
00:25:19,352 --> 00:25:20,787
- But I was training for months.

742
00:25:20,820 --> 00:25:21,688
- Go on.

743
00:25:21,722 --> 00:25:22,888
- [Tom] I wish I was a doctor.

744
00:25:22,922 --> 00:25:25,192
- They've all become fanatics
since Hercules arrived.

745
00:25:25,225 --> 00:25:27,493
They seem to worship
nothing but strength.

746
00:25:27,527 --> 00:25:29,862
- Their studies are neglected
for the glory of the arena.

747
00:25:29,897 --> 00:25:31,330
Isn't that so, Orpheus?

748
00:25:31,363 --> 00:25:32,398
- [Joel] Who are you?

749
00:25:32,432 --> 00:25:34,600
- Yes Laertes, for the
moment, poetry languishes.

750
00:25:34,633 --> 00:25:35,635
- [Tom] Hey, can we
play through?

751
00:25:35,668 --> 00:25:36,870
- And my lyre will
soon sing songs

752
00:25:36,903 --> 00:25:39,172
of nothing but
heroes in battles.

753
00:25:39,172 --> 00:25:40,573
- Well look Tifi, here's Argos.

754
00:25:40,573 --> 00:25:41,808
- He seems to be furious.

755
00:25:41,875 --> 00:25:42,775
- [Crow] I'm furious.

756
00:25:42,808 --> 00:25:43,977
- All of you here in the arena?

757
00:25:44,010 --> 00:25:45,578
And have you all
changed to his ways?

758
00:25:45,612 --> 00:25:48,582
Ha, talk to the men, they
speak only of Hercules.

759
00:25:48,615 --> 00:25:49,582
