1010
00:34:08,680 --> 00:34:11,117
- It may still be you, Hercules.

1011
00:34:11,150 --> 00:34:12,985
- [Tom] Alright boys,
back to the precinct.

1012
00:34:13,018 --> 00:34:13,987
Let's go.

1013
00:34:14,020 --> 00:34:16,522
(siren wailing)

1014
00:34:16,555 --> 00:34:17,623
- [Joel] So, lunch?

1015
00:34:17,657 --> 00:34:20,358
Oh yeah, you're dead, but still.

1016
00:34:22,962 --> 00:34:25,565
- I told you Pelias, I
prophesied doom

1017
00:34:25,598 --> 00:34:27,032
if you didn't send him away.

1018
00:34:27,065 --> 00:34:29,035
- He's dead, my son.

1019
00:34:29,068 --> 00:34:30,302
Oh, cruel gods.

1020
00:34:30,335 --> 00:34:32,070
- Useless complaining
to the gods.

1021
00:34:32,105 --> 00:34:33,138
Plan your revenge now.

1022
00:34:33,172 --> 00:34:33,973
- [Crow] Avoid the rush.

1023
00:34:34,007 --> 00:34:35,575
- Revenge my son, (mumbles).

1024
00:34:35,608 --> 00:34:37,977
I'll make Hercules
suffer the way I suffer.

1025
00:34:38,010 --> 00:34:40,012
- Listen to what I say to you.

1026
00:34:40,045 --> 00:34:41,380
- [Tom] Your tunic's
open in the rear.

1027
00:34:41,413 --> 00:34:43,917
I can see your bike rack.

1028
00:34:43,950 --> 00:34:47,253
- And if you just do that, you
can forget he's invincible.

1029
00:34:47,287 --> 00:34:48,253
- [Man] Your highness.

1030
00:34:48,287 --> 00:34:49,088
- [Joel] Yeah.

1031
00:34:49,122 --> 00:34:50,590
- [Man] Hercules has returned.

1032
00:34:50,623 --> 00:34:53,125
- [Crow] Oh, I'll
alert the media.

1033
00:34:54,327 --> 00:34:58,230
- [Tom] It's Hercules, why
is everything Hercules, ah?

1034
00:34:58,263 --> 00:35:00,232
- [Joel] Hey boss, did
you hear about Hercules?

1035
00:35:00,265 --> 00:35:03,335
- [Crow] Yes, I heard
about Hercules?

1036
00:35:06,405 --> 00:35:07,907
- [Joel] Now what?

1037
00:35:11,577 --> 00:35:13,847
- [Tom] Uh, hi, um, he broke.

1038
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:14,913
Sorry.

1039
00:35:14,947 --> 00:35:17,550
(grunting)

1040
00:35:17,583 --> 00:35:20,920
- [Crow] Could you give
me a hand here?

1041
00:35:24,690 --> 00:35:28,828
- [Joel] Okay, whose
gonna sign for this?

1042
00:35:28,862 --> 00:35:33,032
- [Tom] Careful, I'd recommend
a cool storage place.

1043
00:35:34,933 --> 00:35:38,603
- [Joel] Uh, could I have
his room, dad?

1044
00:35:38,637 --> 00:35:41,373
- [Tom] I love my
dead Greek son.

1045
00:35:42,642 --> 00:35:45,343
- [Group] Our work
here is finished.

1046
00:35:45,377 --> 00:35:48,180
(sobbing)

1047
00:35:48,213 --> 00:35:50,550
- [Tom] Look, no charge, okay?

1048
00:35:50,583 --> 00:35:52,585
- No one requested you go
after the lion.

1049
00:35:52,618 --> 00:35:54,320
- [Joel] He did it on spec.

1050
00:35:54,353 --> 00:35:57,357
- If you hadn't been
so headstrong,

1051
00:35:57,390 --> 00:35:58,657
he would still be alive.

1052
00:35:58,690 --> 00:36:00,793
- [Tom] But any way, it's
still a nice day, huh?

1053
00:36:00,827 --> 00:36:01,827
- The lion is vanquished.

1054
00:36:01,860 --> 00:36:02,962
- [Crow] The lion
takes Vanquish?

1055
00:36:02,995 --> 00:36:06,098
- The parents of his victims
feel grateful, I suppose.

1056
00:36:06,132 --> 00:36:07,767
The danger is past them now.

1057
00:36:07,800 --> 00:36:11,737
- [All] Give us Barabbas,
Barabbas, Barabbas.

1058
00:36:11,770 --> 00:36:13,738
- But it can't placate me.

1059
00:36:13,772 --> 00:36:15,173
- [Joel] Go ahead, let it out,
come on.

1060
00:36:15,207 --> 00:36:17,643
- You want only your glory.

1061
00:36:17,677 --> 00:36:21,247
You brought the gods'
vengeance on my house.

1062
00:36:21,280 --> 00:36:22,615
You'll atone for these things.

1063
00:36:22,648 --> 00:36:23,950
- [Tom] You'll atone
for these things.

1064
00:36:23,983 --> 00:36:26,085
- You fought the lion.

1065
00:36:26,118 --> 00:36:28,253
You'll pay for the things
you believe in.

1066
00:36:28,287 --> 00:36:30,690
You'll do what I order you to.

1067
00:36:30,723 --> 00:36:32,692
And I swear no man
will help you.

1068
00:36:32,725 --> 00:36:33,592
- [Crow] I ain't helpin' him,
you?

1069
00:36:33,625 --> 00:36:34,627
- [Joel] Nope.

1070
00:36:34,660 --> 00:36:35,762
- I charge you to meet
the Cretan Bull in battle

1071
00:36:35,795 --> 00:36:37,263
and may the curse of the
gods be upon you.

1072
00:36:37,297 --> 00:36:38,932
- [Tom] Look, can I get
a word in here?

1073
00:36:38,965 --> 00:36:41,467
- Until you pay for the
blood of Iphitos.

1074
00:36:41,500 --> 00:36:43,468
- [Tom] You are dead,
aren't you?

1075
00:36:43,502 --> 00:36:45,437
(crying)

1076
00:36:45,470 --> 00:36:48,473
- [Joel] Oh, what a
crummy 4th of July.

1077
00:36:48,507 --> 00:36:51,010
(loud marching footsteps)

1078
00:36:51,043 --> 00:36:53,145
- [Crow] Sorry ma'am,
got another show.

1079
00:36:53,178 --> 00:36:54,247
Just, ah, thanks.

1080
00:36:54,280 --> 00:36:58,117
- [Tom] Oh, saw him move,
just kidding, sorry.

1081
00:36:59,352 --> 00:37:01,953
- [Joel] Well, I see my chance.

1082
00:37:03,622 --> 00:37:05,725
- [Crow] So, uh, why the
long face, kidding of course,

1083
00:37:05,758 --> 00:37:06,958
just breakin' the ice.

1084
00:37:06,992 --> 00:37:10,597
- Iole, I didn't want to
speak out against your father.

1085
00:37:10,630 --> 00:37:14,300
But his punishment's unfair,
and his accusations unjust.

1086
00:37:14,300 --> 00:37:15,400
- [Tom] He's just so bogus.

1087
00:37:15,433 --> 00:37:16,602
- Yes, I know.

1088
00:37:16,635 --> 00:37:18,938
Hercules must listen
only to the gods.

1089
00:37:19,005 --> 00:37:21,440
Because he cannot know
the suffering of a woman.

1090
00:37:21,507 --> 00:37:23,708
- [Joel] Oh, yeah, it's
a woman thing.

1091
00:37:23,708 --> 00:37:24,810
- Listen to me, Iole.

1092
00:37:24,843 --> 00:37:26,645
- I don't want to.

1093
00:37:26,678 --> 00:37:27,913
Go away.

1094
00:37:27,947 --> 00:37:30,115
(sobbing)

1095
00:37:32,618 --> 00:37:36,788
- [Crow] Maybe I'll call
Sampson, see what he's up to.

1096
00:37:39,225 --> 00:37:42,060
- [Joel] But she likes me,
really.

1097
00:37:43,997 --> 00:37:46,965
- [Tom] Wait, wait, you
guys, the party's not over,

1098
00:37:46,998 --> 00:37:48,533
I got plenty of cocktails left

1099
00:37:48,567 --> 00:37:50,168
with the little
umbrellas in 'em.

1100
00:37:50,202 --> 00:37:51,003
Come on.

1101
00:37:53,172 --> 00:37:54,540
- [Crow] Well I'm
still immortal,

1102
00:37:54,573 --> 00:37:57,477
they can't take that
away from me.

1103
00:37:57,510 --> 00:38:01,013
- [Joel] Oh yeah, I'll
clean up the lion.

1104
00:38:04,450 --> 00:38:08,453
- [Tom] James A. Michener's
Adventures in Hercules.

1105
00:38:08,487 --> 00:38:09,555
- [Joel] Looks like he's doin'
real good,

1106
00:38:09,588 --> 00:38:12,090
he's got a paper route.

1107
00:38:12,123 --> 00:38:16,262
- [Crow] Oh dang, on top of
everything, my house is on fire.

1108
00:38:17,228 --> 00:38:20,098
- [Tom] Shane, come back Shane.

1109
00:38:20,132 --> 00:38:23,968
- [Joel] Hey, what's for dinner,
Hop Sing?

1110
00:38:24,003 --> 00:38:26,072
- [Crow] There will be patches
of scattered god today,

1111
00:38:26,105 --> 00:38:26,938
followed by--

1112
00:38:26,972 --> 00:38:29,375
- Why did Iphitos have to die?

1113
00:38:29,408 --> 00:38:30,977
Answer me, Sybil.

1114
00:38:31,010 --> 00:38:32,578
I cannot understand.

1115
00:38:32,612 --> 00:38:33,812
I'm greatly confused.

1116
00:38:33,845 --> 00:38:36,248
A man I could crush with
one hand gives me an order,

1117
00:38:36,282 --> 00:38:37,917
a woman humiliates me.

1118
00:38:37,950 --> 00:38:40,285
- It is not you who is to blame,
Hercules.

1119
00:38:40,318 --> 00:38:42,722
Iphitos died simply because
he was not meant to be

1120
00:38:42,755 --> 00:38:43,822
King of Julco.

1121
00:38:43,855 --> 00:38:45,490
- [Joel] Uh, will you
hand me the extinguisher?

1122
00:38:45,523 --> 00:38:48,160
- Now the gods assign a
new labor to you.

1123
00:38:48,193 --> 00:38:50,062
They want you to go out
and chance your fate

1124
00:38:50,095 --> 00:38:51,363
against the Cretan Bull.

1125
00:38:51,397 --> 00:38:52,398
- Enough.

1126
00:38:52,432 --> 00:38:54,367
I'm tired of doing all
of these senseless things

1127
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:55,500
for the gods.

1128
00:38:55,533 --> 00:38:57,637
When will I be worthy
in the eyes of the gods?

1129
00:38:57,670 --> 00:38:58,670
- [Crow] I'm in over
my head here.

1130
00:38:58,703 --> 00:39:00,005
- The hour of your
fate is nearing.

1131
00:39:00,038 --> 00:39:01,807
Don't rebel against it.

1132
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:03,542
- Now listen to me.

1133
00:39:03,575 --> 00:39:05,712
These changes have happened
to me in the last few days.

1134
00:39:05,745 --> 00:39:06,545
- [Tom] Male menopause.

1135
00:39:06,578 --> 00:39:08,913
- Iole, the way they
punished me.

1136
00:39:08,947 --> 00:39:11,850
All of these things help
me to feel in another way.

1137
00:39:11,883 --> 00:39:12,885
- [Joel] All tingly.

1138
00:39:12,918 --> 00:39:14,453
- I can't stand being superior.

1139
00:39:14,487 --> 00:39:18,190
Let me experience the
real things, love or hate.

1140
00:39:18,223 --> 00:39:20,625
- Those are mortal states,
Hercules.

1141
00:39:20,658 --> 00:39:22,695
- If it's my immortality
making me unhappy,

1142
00:39:22,728 --> 00:39:24,430
then I'll do without it.

1143
00:39:24,463 --> 00:39:26,198
- That's dangerous, Hercules.

1144
00:39:26,232 --> 00:39:28,667
Don't you know how foolish
you'd be to renounce it?

1145
00:39:28,700 --> 00:39:30,702
To be born a man and to
see everything die

1146
00:39:30,737 --> 00:39:32,505
is not to be immortal.

1147
00:39:32,538 --> 00:39:33,005
Stay as you are.

1148
00:39:33,038 --> 00:39:34,173
Be a god.

1149
00:39:34,207 --> 00:39:37,743
Don't exchange immortality
for fear, pain, and sorrow.

1150
00:39:37,777 --> 00:39:40,045
- I want to live like
any other mortal man.

1151
00:39:40,078 --> 00:39:41,180
- [Crow] Oh, brother.

1152
00:39:41,213 --> 00:39:42,848
- It's my prayer to
have a family.

1153
00:39:42,882 --> 00:39:44,083
- [Tom] A nice
two-bedroom apartment.

1154
00:39:44,117 --> 00:39:45,918
- I want children of my own.

1155
00:39:45,952 --> 00:39:47,687
- [Joel] Herc is a '90s woman.

1156
00:39:47,720 --> 00:39:49,222
- To see your
children growing up.

1157
00:39:49,255 --> 00:39:50,555
- Pass on, Hercules.

1158
00:39:50,588 --> 00:39:51,623
- [Crow] You're barren, pal.

1159
00:39:51,657 --> 00:39:54,127
- It's all as you ask.

1160
00:39:54,160 --> 00:39:56,895
Now you shall have to
confront your future

1161
00:39:56,928 --> 00:40:00,632
and fight using only
your own forces.

1162
00:40:00,665 --> 00:40:03,935
Mortal victories or
you'll be defeated.

1163
00:40:12,778 --> 00:40:14,012
- Uh, Joel?

1164
00:40:14,045 --> 00:40:16,882
You remember the group Hamilton,
Joe, Frank and Reynolds?

1165
00:40:16,915 --> 00:40:19,017
- Oh sure, of course I do,
they had uh,

1166
00:40:19,050 --> 00:40:22,220
two huge chart-busting hits
when I was a kid in the '70s.

1167
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:23,955
- What were they?

1168
00:40:23,988 --> 00:40:26,558
- Oh um, well the first one was

1169
00:40:27,827 --> 00:40:29,595
Don't pull your love out
on me, baby, remember?

1170
00:40:29,628 --> 00:40:32,665
Don't pull your love
out on me, baby

1171
00:40:32,698 --> 00:40:33,565
- Oh sure, I remember that.

1172
00:40:33,598 --> 00:40:35,400
Now what was the other hit?

1173
00:40:35,433 --> 00:40:39,138
- Oh uh, I don't really
remember the second one,

1174
00:40:39,172 --> 00:40:41,873
except that it
sounded a lot like.

1175
00:40:41,907 --> 00:40:44,543
- [All] Don't pull your love
out on me, baby, right see.

1176
00:40:44,577 --> 00:40:45,945
- How many members did
that band have?

1177
00:40:45,978 --> 00:40:47,412
- Oh come on, Crow, that's easy.

1178
00:40:47,445 --> 00:40:50,715
They were a quartet, Hamilton,
Joe, Frank and Reynolds.

1179
00:40:50,748 --> 00:40:51,550
- Really?

1180
00:40:51,583 --> 00:40:52,383
I always thought
they were a duo,

1181
00:40:52,417 --> 00:40:54,520
Hamilton Joe Frank and Reynolds.

1182
00:40:54,553 --> 00:40:56,188
- No, you guys, it was a trio.

1183
00:40:56,222 --> 00:40:59,492
Hamilton Joe, Frank
and Reynolds.

1184
00:40:59,525 --> 00:41:01,027
- Wait, they were a quintet.

1185
00:41:01,060 --> 00:41:02,027
- How do ya figure that?

1186
00:41:02,060 --> 00:41:05,230
- Well, Hamilton, Joe,
Frank, Ann, Reynolds.

1187
00:41:05,263 --> 00:41:09,802
- But maybe if Ann Reynolds
is one person, Tom,

1188
00:41:09,835 --> 00:41:11,337
that would lead us
all right back

1189
00:41:11,370 --> 00:41:12,705
to the whole trio theory.

1190
00:41:12,738 --> 00:41:13,472
- Oh.

1191
00:41:13,505 --> 00:41:14,707
- Well, with names like that,

1192
00:41:14,740 --> 00:41:17,375
why the heck did they even
name the band after themselves?

1193
00:41:17,408 --> 00:41:19,778
Hamilton, Joe, Frank and
Reynolds does not exactly

1194
00:41:19,812 --> 00:41:22,548
roll off the tongue, like
Dino, Desi and Billy.

1195
00:41:22,582 --> 00:41:24,283
- Joel, do you think
we'll ever find the answer

1196
00:41:24,317 --> 00:41:27,085
to the Hamilton, Joe,
Frank and Reynolds mystery?

1197
00:41:27,118 --> 00:41:29,053
- Well, who can answer my
young friends?

1198
00:41:29,087 --> 00:41:30,990
Who can really answer?

1199
00:41:31,023 --> 00:41:32,490
- Well, Hamilton, Joe,
Frank and Reynolds.

1200
00:41:32,525 --> 00:41:33,892
(beeping)
(screaming)

1201
00:41:33,925 --> 00:41:37,462
(clacking)
(thrumming)

1202
00:41:37,495 --> 00:41:39,832
(rolling)
(sliding)

1203
00:41:39,865 --> 00:41:41,967
(crackling)
(creaking)

1204
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:43,602
(sliding)
(slamming)

1205
00:41:43,635 --> 00:41:44,703
- Therefore you may
have come here.

1206
00:41:44,737 --> 00:41:45,537
- [Joel] Good morning.

1207
00:41:45,570 --> 00:41:46,838
- Only to defraud me.

1208
00:41:46,872 --> 00:41:49,140
- I myself heard Chiron
talk about the fleece.

1209
00:41:49,173 --> 00:41:52,678
- Your words can't influence
me in what I must do.

1210
00:41:52,712 --> 00:41:56,115
You've brought enough
unhappiness to my house.

1211
00:41:56,148 --> 00:41:57,515
Do you wanna take my throne now?

1212
00:41:57,550 --> 00:41:59,718
- Well, maybe this will
convince Pelias.

1213
00:41:59,752 --> 00:42:00,852
- [Tom] Would you just.

1214
00:42:00,887 --> 00:42:03,255
(scuffling)

1215
00:42:03,288 --> 00:42:06,458
- [Crow] Ooh, look at
the pins on him.

1216
00:42:07,292 --> 00:42:10,295
- [Joel] Athletes foot, ew.

1217
00:42:10,328 --> 00:42:11,697
- [Tom] Great legs,
whadya think, huh?

1218
00:42:11,730 --> 00:42:14,132
(chattering)

1219
00:42:14,165 --> 00:42:17,102
- [Crow] I'd kill for
those ankles.

1220
00:42:18,337 --> 00:42:19,305
- If I may speak,

1221
00:42:19,338 --> 00:42:21,273
I think this discussion
is a waste of time.

1222
00:42:21,307 --> 00:42:22,608
- [Joel] No, Larry, you may not.

1223
00:42:22,642 --> 00:42:24,075
- If this is Jason and he
tells the truth,

1224
00:42:24,108 --> 00:42:25,710
then we must ask the
gods to prove it.

1225
00:42:25,743 --> 00:42:28,380
- The Colchis is a long
journey, but if we persist

1226
00:42:28,413 --> 00:42:30,382
and take this voyage
as I suggest,

1227
00:42:30,415 --> 00:42:32,483
we might find the truth
about King Aeson's death.

1228
00:42:32,517 --> 00:42:33,685
- [Tom] Howard Johnson is right.

1229
00:42:33,718 --> 00:42:34,953
- I feels the gods favor us

1230
00:42:34,987 --> 00:42:36,188
piercing the mysterious Colchis.

1231
00:42:36,222 --> 00:42:37,322
- [All] Ew.

1232
00:42:37,355 --> 00:42:39,825
- It's perilous and all
our men shall need courage.

1233
00:42:39,858 --> 00:42:40,858
- [Tom] Courage.

1234
00:42:40,892 --> 00:42:44,397
- For you see, for years
we wanted an opportunity,

1235
00:42:44,430 --> 00:42:46,165
and now know the adventure
for which Argo's ship

1236
00:42:46,198 --> 00:42:46,698
was destined.

1237
00:42:46,732 --> 00:42:47,933
- [Joel] Who is he?

1238
00:42:47,967 --> 00:42:50,668
- The poets will write about
this in all the years to come.

1239
00:42:50,702 --> 00:42:51,837
- [Crow] Like Rod McKuen?

1240
00:42:51,870 --> 00:42:53,872
- How we found the
fleece of gold

1241
00:42:53,905 --> 00:42:56,142
or disappeared in the
silence beneath us.

1242
00:42:56,208 --> 00:42:57,643
Let the people appraise
the legitimate heir

1243
00:42:57,710 --> 00:42:59,512
to the glorious throne of Julco.

1244
00:42:59,545 --> 00:43:00,947
- [All] Hail, Dorothy.

1245
00:43:01,013 --> 00:43:02,247
- We must be able to
know who he is

1246
00:43:02,313 --> 00:43:03,715
the day we come back.

1247
00:43:03,715 --> 00:43:05,850
- Orpheus is right, I
shall prepare the boat.

1248
00:43:05,917 --> 00:43:06,718
- [Joel] What boat?

1249
00:43:06,718 --> 00:43:07,518
- And I shall go, too.

1250
00:43:07,552 --> 00:43:08,720
- I also.

1251
00:43:08,753 --> 00:43:09,622
- We'll go.

1252
00:43:09,622 --> 00:43:10,355
- [Tom] Et tu.

1253
00:43:10,422 --> 00:43:11,257
- Do as you must.

1254
00:43:11,290 --> 00:43:13,025
The gods have willed you
to decide this.

1255
00:43:13,058 --> 00:43:14,660
- [Crow] Rip Torn, ladies
and gentlemen.

1256
00:43:14,693 --> 00:43:16,862
- But don't expect me
to wait here.

1257
00:43:16,895 --> 00:43:19,732
Tortured by doubt for the
little time that I have.

1258
00:43:19,765 --> 00:43:20,898
- [Joel] And I'm not
gonna pick you up, either.

1259
00:43:20,932 --> 00:43:22,533
- You have three months
to come back.

1260
00:43:22,567 --> 00:43:24,303
Not one day more.

1261
00:43:24,337 --> 00:43:25,770
- [Tom] You kids will be
the death of me.

1262
00:43:25,803 --> 00:43:28,140
- [Crow] I need a salty dog.

1263
00:43:29,207 --> 00:43:32,110
- [Joel] Has anybody
seen my heels?

1264
00:43:32,143 --> 00:43:33,978
- [Crow] Eyes front, Carl.

1265
00:43:34,012 --> 00:43:35,713
- Be assured of our help.

1266
00:43:35,747 --> 00:43:36,782
- What he says is true.

1267
00:43:36,815 --> 00:43:37,615
- You can count on me.

1268
00:43:37,650 --> 00:43:38,850
- You do look like King Aeson.

1269
00:43:38,883 --> 00:43:41,787
- Of course, because
he is Jason.

1270
00:43:41,820 --> 00:43:43,555
- Has anyone spoken of Ulysses?

1271
00:43:43,588 --> 00:43:44,890
That's me, I'll introduce you.

1272
00:43:44,923 --> 00:43:46,358
It's so nice that
you'll let me go.

1273
00:43:46,392 --> 00:43:47,325
(laughter)

1274
00:43:47,358 --> 00:43:48,927
- [Tom] Live from the
Fontainebleau Hotel.

1275
00:43:48,960 --> 00:43:49,862
- Iole.

1276
00:43:49,895 --> 00:43:50,862
- [Crow] Oh, that dress,
melts my fillings.

1277
00:43:50,895 --> 00:43:51,830
(leering)

1278
00:43:51,863 --> 00:43:52,563
- What do you want of me?

1279
00:43:52,597 --> 00:43:53,798
- [Joel] Do you have a quarter?

1280
00:43:53,832 --> 00:43:55,967
- [Hercules] Don't think I'm
being hostile to your father.

1281
00:43:56,002 --> 00:43:57,635
- Isn't that funny?

1282
00:43:57,670 --> 00:43:58,870
Then what should I think?

1283
00:43:58,903 --> 00:44:00,872
- [Hercules] I'm only
searching for the truth.

1284
00:44:00,905 --> 00:44:01,940
- [Tom] You can't
handle the truth.

1285
00:44:01,973 --> 00:44:03,142
- Truth?

1286
00:44:03,175 --> 00:44:04,777
I feel the truth no longer
matters after what you've done

1287
00:44:04,810 --> 00:44:05,910
to him in there.

1288
00:44:05,943 --> 00:44:07,212
- Listen to what I have to say.

1289
00:44:07,245 --> 00:44:09,648
What I've done is for you.

1290
00:44:09,682 --> 00:44:12,083
- I don't belong to you now.

1291
00:44:12,117 --> 00:44:14,185
You listen to the
words of Orpheus.

1292
00:44:14,218 --> 00:44:16,255
There's a new mission to begin.

1293
00:44:16,288 --> 00:44:18,257
One will be covered
with success.

1294
00:44:18,290 --> 00:44:20,325
Follow the one you name Jason,
then.

1295
00:44:20,358 --> 00:44:22,962
And come back victorious,
like the adventurer you are.

1296
00:44:22,995 --> 00:44:24,095
- [Crow] Whoa, back off.

1297
00:44:24,128 --> 00:44:25,663
- Do you remember what you
said the first day we met?

1298
00:44:25,697 --> 00:44:26,665
- [Tom] Oh, you mean ew.

1299
00:44:26,698 --> 00:44:28,167
- That couldn't be happy
as long as the mystery

1300
00:44:28,200 --> 00:44:31,002
of your uncle's death
couldn't be cleared up.

1301
00:44:31,037 --> 00:44:33,405
Listen, Iole, it's our
destiny to solve it.

1302
00:44:33,438 --> 00:44:34,540
- No Hercules.

1303
00:44:34,573 --> 00:44:36,375
Your destiny is not mine.

1304
00:44:36,408 --> 00:44:37,710
- [Joel] Meh, better take a jump

1305
00:44:37,743 --> 00:44:39,310
in that cold fountain, Herc.

1306
00:44:39,343 --> 00:44:42,213
- [Crow] Later that same day.

1307
00:44:42,247 --> 00:44:44,082
- They'll succeed
I'm sure of it.

1308
00:44:44,115 --> 00:44:45,783
They'll return with the
Golden Fleece.

1309
00:44:45,817 --> 00:44:47,485
I'll be accused.

1310
00:44:47,518 --> 00:44:48,520
They'll kill us all.

1311
00:44:48,553 --> 00:44:50,788
- [All] Woo, yay, yes, yes,
very nice.

1312
00:44:50,822 --> 00:44:52,792
- Yes, because she's mine.

1313
00:44:52,825 --> 00:44:54,960
- It started because of
that man without a sandal.

1314
00:44:54,993 --> 00:44:56,262
- That's enough, Pelias.

1315
00:44:56,295 --> 00:44:57,797
- These lamentations
aren't going to save you.

1316
00:44:57,830 --> 00:44:58,630
- Alright, then.

1317
00:44:58,663 --> 00:44:59,698
Help us.

1318
00:44:59,732 --> 00:45:01,600
Do you know any way to save us?

1319
00:45:01,633 --> 00:45:03,235
I'm ready to do it.

1320
00:45:04,503 --> 00:45:08,840
- If Jason's murdered and
since your son is dead,

1321
00:45:08,873 --> 00:45:13,145
you must see, you can't expect
your daughter to rule alone.

1322
00:45:13,178 --> 00:45:14,045
- No.

1323
00:45:14,078 --> 00:45:15,780
You shall never marry Iole.

1324
00:45:15,813 --> 00:45:16,648
Monster.

1325
00:45:17,883 --> 00:45:20,518
- Their craft's almost
ready to sail.

1326
00:45:20,552 --> 00:45:22,687
I could be on it.

1327
00:45:22,720 --> 00:45:24,757
Better think it over.

1328
00:45:24,790 --> 00:45:25,723
Goodnight.

1329
00:45:25,757 --> 00:45:28,193
- [Crow] And now, funny
man Morty Gunty.

1330
00:45:28,227 --> 00:45:30,362
- [Joel] Well, you wanna
eat or anything?

1331
00:45:30,395 --> 00:45:33,165
- [Tom] Nah, I'm
gonna eat alone.

1332
00:45:38,503 --> 00:45:40,605
- [Crow] Nice day for it.

1333
00:45:44,008 --> 00:45:46,745
- [Joel] Looks like it's a
big, brawny, hairy, glistening,

1334
00:45:46,778 --> 00:45:48,613
two-fisted, manly day.

1335
00:45:50,048 --> 00:45:52,583
- [Tom] What a cheap cruise.

1336
00:45:52,617 --> 00:45:56,020
- [Crow] I wanna be mortal,
what was I thinking?

1337
00:45:56,053 --> 00:45:59,858
(singing in foreign language)

1338
00:46:00,792 --> 00:46:02,928
- [Joel] Dennis Day?

1339
00:46:02,962 --> 00:46:04,963
- [Crow] Any day.

1340
00:46:04,997 --> 00:46:06,432
- Hercules, why don't you sing?

1341
00:46:06,465 --> 00:46:07,398
- [Tom] I'd rather not
talk about it.

1342
00:46:07,432 --> 00:46:09,835
- Wager it's Iole, hey?

1343
00:46:09,868 --> 00:46:12,470
- [Crow] What was that
supposed to mean?

1344
00:46:12,503 --> 00:46:15,040
- You're not the man to
act like that.

1345
00:46:15,073 --> 00:46:16,442
First they're saying.

1346
00:46:16,475 --> 00:46:18,343
- [Joel] Oh, why did I
sit with this guy?

1347
00:46:18,377 --> 00:46:20,112
- Then begins that
jealous feeling.

1348
00:46:20,145 --> 00:46:21,913
That passes after
you're married,

1349
00:46:21,947 --> 00:46:24,082
because then you're too
tired to be jealous.

1350
00:46:24,115 --> 00:46:25,050
- [Crow] Shut up.

1351
00:46:25,083 --> 00:46:26,017
Steward.

1352
00:46:26,050 --> 00:46:29,588
- [Tom] Abe Lincoln
looks cheesed here, huh?

1353
00:46:29,622 --> 00:46:34,092
(singing in foreign language)

1354
00:46:34,125 --> 00:46:36,795
- [Joel] What, did Herc
get on a swing choir barge?

1355
00:46:36,828 --> 00:46:40,398
- Here comes the wind,
get to the sails.

1356
00:46:40,432 --> 00:46:41,633
- [Crow] Oh good, this
is the fun part.

1357
00:46:41,667 --> 00:46:44,770
I like this a lot
better than rowing.

1358
00:46:47,405 --> 00:46:49,742
- [Tom] What are they doing?

1359
00:46:50,975 --> 00:46:54,412
(squealing and grunting)

1360
00:46:59,552 --> 00:47:01,853
- [Crow] The mighty
canvas, like a giant skin,

1361
00:47:01,887 --> 00:47:04,055
hoisted aloft by sinewy hands.

1362
00:47:04,088 --> 00:47:05,390
- Time goes slowly here at sea.

1363
00:47:05,423 --> 00:47:08,127
I think I'll start a calendar.

1364
00:47:08,160 --> 00:47:09,628
One notch for each day.

1365
00:47:09,662 --> 00:47:10,628
- [Joel] Well, now that's
a good system.

1366
00:47:10,662 --> 00:47:12,497
I would of done something
like three notches,

1367
00:47:12,530 --> 00:47:14,265
but he simplified it.

1368
00:47:20,305 --> 00:47:22,607
- [Tom] You'd think that
they'd be further away by now.

1369
00:47:22,640 --> 00:47:25,710
They're barely past the dock.

1370
00:47:25,743 --> 00:47:28,880
- [Joel] Well, no plot
on the horizon.

1371
00:47:29,882 --> 00:47:33,952
- [Crow] I wonder what I'm
thinking about?

1372
00:47:33,985 --> 00:47:38,190
- [Tom] Where do you want
these place settings, ma'am?

1373
00:47:39,423 --> 00:47:43,128
- [Joel] Um, will you
be checking out today?

1374
00:47:43,162 --> 00:47:44,730
- You don't speak anymore,

1375
00:47:44,763 --> 00:47:46,432
you just keep looking out there.

1376
00:47:46,465 --> 00:47:47,265
- [Crow] Keep it up.

1377
00:47:47,298 --> 00:47:48,233
- We're all sad, too.

1378
00:47:48,267 --> 00:47:49,735
- They never went this
far before, I guess.

1379
00:47:49,768 --> 00:47:51,068
- That's enough.

1380
00:47:51,102 --> 00:47:54,272
- [Tom] Gee, sorry for
supporting you.

1381
00:47:56,073 --> 00:47:57,375
- [Joel] If you're going
to do an intervention,

1382
00:47:57,408 --> 00:48:01,447
you're gonna have to be
more persistent than that.

1383
00:48:02,513 --> 00:48:07,285
- [All] Man on the floor,
man on the floor, man.

1384
00:48:07,318 --> 00:48:09,187
- [Crow] Now what did I
come in here for?

1385
00:48:09,220 --> 00:48:10,322
Oh yeah.

1386
00:48:10,355 --> 00:48:11,188
No.

1387
00:48:13,792 --> 00:48:15,493
- You wait so anxiously.

1388
00:48:15,527 --> 00:48:17,495
While my fate is decided.

1389
00:48:17,528 --> 00:48:18,963
- Yes, father.

1390
00:48:18,997 --> 00:48:20,965
We ask for only peace of mind.

1391
00:48:20,998 --> 00:48:21,800
- [Tom] Oh, and the car.

1392
00:48:21,833 --> 00:48:23,535
- And if this boy is
really Jason?

1393
00:48:23,568 --> 00:48:26,070
- [Crow] Well, he claims
to be, but damn if I know.

1394
00:48:26,103 --> 00:48:28,740
- The throne is a burden.

1395
00:48:28,773 --> 00:48:30,908
You even wanted to give it up,
you said.

1396
00:48:30,942 --> 00:48:33,645
- To begin over again, my child.

1397
00:48:33,678 --> 00:48:35,080
No I can't do it.

1398
00:48:35,113 --> 00:48:36,882
I know the gods will aid you

1399
00:48:36,915 --> 00:48:37,748
and Hercules.

1400
00:48:37,782 --> 00:48:38,550
Don't say that.

1401
00:48:38,583 --> 00:48:40,218
- [Crow] Oh, daddy.

1402
00:48:41,218 --> 00:48:44,422
No, Iole, I would like
to wipe him your mind.

1403
00:48:44,455 --> 00:48:46,625
- [Joel] Um, I'm not a hugger.

1404
00:48:47,960 --> 00:48:49,527
- [Crow] Well you probably
should have thought about that

1405
00:48:49,527 --> 00:48:50,828
before we left.

1406
00:48:55,133 --> 00:48:57,702
- [Joel] There go the dumbest
group of guys you'll ever see.

1407
00:48:57,735 --> 00:48:58,737
Look at 'em.

1408
00:49:00,005 --> 00:49:01,707
- [Tom] Twelve angry Greeks.

1409
00:49:01,740 --> 00:49:03,975
- Well get moving, get to work.

1410
00:49:04,008 --> 00:49:05,010
- [Crow] Geez, you've got
to take orders

1411
00:49:05,043 --> 00:49:07,612
from Pete Townshend in a dress.

1412
00:49:10,615 --> 00:49:11,483
- Until later.

1413
00:49:11,517 --> 00:49:12,783
- [Joel] Yeah don't
look at our butts.

1414
00:49:12,817 --> 00:49:13,752
- [Crow] Okay.

1415
00:49:13,785 --> 00:49:14,953
- [Tom] Oh boy (laughter),

1416
00:49:14,987 --> 00:49:16,888
you know the bigger they
are, the nicer they are.

1417
00:49:16,922 --> 00:49:17,722
- [Crow] Their butts?

1418
00:49:17,755 --> 00:49:18,557
- [Tom] No, no.

1419
00:49:18,590 --> 00:49:20,158
- [Crow] Oh.

1420
00:49:20,192 --> 00:49:21,192
- [Tom] Oh, there you are.

1421
00:49:21,225 --> 00:49:23,662
(chattering)

1422
00:49:25,997 --> 00:49:26,865
- [Crow] Do you like Hercules?

1423
00:49:26,898 --> 00:49:29,233
I think it's kind of a jerk.

1424
00:49:32,970 --> 00:49:34,773
- Let's keep together.

1425
00:49:34,807 --> 00:49:36,307
Better take this path.

1426
00:49:36,342 --> 00:49:37,808
- [Tom] Okay we'll take
this other path.

1427
00:49:37,842 --> 00:49:41,413
- [Joel] No I said
stay together.

1428
00:49:41,447 --> 00:49:44,582
C&H pure cane sugar

1429
00:49:46,183 --> 00:49:48,520
- [Crow] I can quit anytime.

1430
00:49:49,722 --> 00:49:52,023
- [Joel] It's a whoopie plant.

1431
00:49:52,057 --> 00:49:53,425
- [Crow] Guys, wait for me.

1432
00:49:53,458 --> 00:49:56,227
(menacing music)

1433
00:50:06,905 --> 00:50:09,908
- [Joel] Attack of the
Mary Martins.

1434
00:50:10,975 --> 00:50:13,445
- [Tom] Oh no, we're captured.

1435
00:50:13,478 --> 00:50:15,413
- [Crow] Joel what was
that shot about?

1436
00:50:15,447 --> 00:50:16,247
- Stay there.

1437
00:50:16,280 --> 00:50:18,417
What do you want on this island?

1438
00:50:18,450 --> 00:50:20,385
- We presumed the
island was deserted.

1439
00:50:20,418 --> 00:50:23,722
Some of us landed to find
water and stock up provisions.

1440
00:50:23,755 --> 00:50:26,290
Be assured our
intentions are peaceful.

1441
00:50:26,323 --> 00:50:28,160
- Throw down your arms
and follow us.

1442
00:50:28,193 --> 00:50:29,862
Queen Antea shall decide.

1443
00:50:29,895 --> 00:50:31,497
- [Tom] We

1444
00:50:31,530 --> 00:50:32,363
surrender.

1445
00:50:35,967 --> 00:50:38,203
(footsteps crunching)

1446
00:50:38,237 --> 00:50:38,903
- Ooh.

1447
00:50:39,938 --> 00:50:41,072
- [Crow] Oh just think
what they could of hit

1448
00:50:41,105 --> 00:50:43,242
if they felt like it.

1449
00:50:43,275 --> 00:50:45,810
- [Tom] Oh come on, they
could never do that again,

1450
00:50:45,843 --> 00:50:46,945
not in a million years.

1451
00:50:46,978 --> 00:50:47,812
Oh, doh.

1452
00:50:49,547 --> 00:50:53,385
- [Crow] Even the archers
are beautiful.

1453
00:50:53,418 --> 00:50:54,618
- Why not?

1454
00:50:54,652 --> 00:50:56,455
Might prove interesting.

1455
00:50:56,488 --> 00:50:58,523
(metal clattering)

1456
00:50:58,557 --> 00:51:01,025
- [Joel] Not the tunics, guys.

1457
00:51:02,860 --> 00:51:03,895
- Follow me.

1458
00:51:03,928 --> 00:51:08,032
Where I go, what I am,
who I know

1459
00:51:08,065 --> 00:51:10,368
- [Joel] Ho, ho, it's a
wacky sitcom.

1460
00:51:10,402 --> 00:51:12,937
- [Tom] Or a wacky satyricon.

1461
00:51:12,970 --> 00:51:17,208
- [Crow] Voon, hey,
Skipper, look what I found.

1462
00:51:17,242 --> 00:51:19,010
- Say what your name is.

1463
00:51:19,043 --> 00:51:21,547
- [Tom] Come here often?

1464
00:51:21,580 --> 00:51:22,780
- [Crow] Isn't
everybody here phony?

1465
00:51:22,813 --> 00:51:24,148
- Don't you ever talk?

1466
00:51:24,182 --> 00:51:27,252
- [Joel] She's an
Ellen Jamesian.

1467
00:51:27,285 --> 00:51:28,987
- I think it's
unbelievable that at 60

1468
00:51:29,020 --> 00:51:31,490
I'm taking part in an
adventure like this one.

1469
00:51:31,523 --> 00:51:33,692
(choking)

1470
00:51:37,195 --> 00:51:38,095
- So whether they're
real alright.

1471
00:51:38,130 --> 00:51:39,363
I always thought it
was a legend,

1472
00:51:39,397 --> 00:51:41,332
the kind of nonsense
invented by poets.

1473
00:51:41,365 --> 00:51:42,200
- [Crow] Yeah, we
hear that a lot.

1474
00:51:42,233 --> 00:51:42,867
- What do you mean?

1475
00:51:42,900 --> 00:51:43,868
Who are they?

1476
00:51:43,902 --> 00:51:45,470
- They are the Amazons,
if you want to know.

1477
00:51:45,503 --> 00:51:46,872
The population is female.

1478
00:51:46,905 --> 00:51:47,938
Absolutely all girls.

1479
00:51:47,972 --> 00:51:48,840
- [Crow] Women.

1480
00:51:48,873 --> 00:51:50,675
- A society similar to the bees.

1481
00:51:50,708 --> 00:51:52,977
- Did you ever hear how
the drones finish?

1482
00:51:53,010 --> 00:51:53,812
- Who finish?

1483
00:51:53,845 --> 00:51:55,080
- Yes, the male bees
of the tribe.

1484
00:51:55,113 --> 00:51:58,750
The females kill them
at the mating season.

1485
00:51:58,783 --> 00:52:00,285
- Look at that.

1486
00:52:00,318 --> 00:52:01,687
- [Joel] It's us.

1487
00:52:01,720 --> 00:52:02,953
- And only men.

1488
00:52:04,255 --> 00:52:07,792
- [Crow] It's the Andrea
Dworkin Memorial Cemetery.

1489
00:52:07,825 --> 00:52:10,462
- [Tom] So you came to island
for food and provisions.

1490
00:52:10,495 --> 00:52:13,532
- Landed here, loved here
and died here.

1491
00:52:13,565 --> 00:52:16,267
- [Joel] Sounds okay to me.

1492
00:52:16,300 --> 00:52:17,068
- A pity.

1493
00:52:18,068 --> 00:52:21,172
- [Tom] That's great,
maybe we should run.

1494
