Schools out for summer

2222
01:23:39,315 --> 01:23:43,720
- [Crow] Well, that chain thing
is still workin' real well.

2223
01:23:43,753 --> 01:23:45,855
- [Tom] This morning a
lone chainman terrorized

2224
01:23:45,888 --> 01:23:49,225
downtown Athens, no
motive was apparent.

2225
01:23:50,993 --> 01:23:51,862
- [Joel] Oh, not this again.

2226
01:23:51,895 --> 01:23:53,763
Any time something
doesn't go his way.

2227
01:23:53,797 --> 01:23:57,400
- [Crow] This is how he
always closes his act.

2228
01:23:57,433 --> 01:23:58,402
- [Tom] Is that a
supporting beam?

2229
01:23:58,435 --> 01:23:59,835
Good, that'll do.

2230
01:24:05,242 --> 01:24:07,477
(groaning)

2231
01:24:14,183 --> 01:24:18,353
The National Guard was called
in to help quell the violence.

2232
01:24:20,590 --> 01:24:22,658
(groaning)

2233
01:24:22,692 --> 01:24:27,563
- [Crow] Hey, Herc, we were
coming to congratulate you.

2234
01:24:27,597 --> 01:24:29,232
- [Joel] Ah, Mr. Hercules,
they just surrendered

2235
01:24:29,265 --> 01:24:30,767
and gave us the palace.

2236
01:24:30,800 --> 01:24:31,935
- [Crow] Oops.

2237
01:24:31,968 --> 01:24:36,105
- [Tom] We probably should
have gotten out first, huh?

2238
01:24:38,775 --> 01:24:40,277
- [Crow] Oh man, if this
were in sense around,

2239
01:24:40,310 --> 01:24:41,110
this would be so great.

2240
01:24:41,143 --> 01:24:43,813
- [Joel] Well, we could vibrate.

2241
01:24:47,383 --> 01:24:48,452
Alright, we're leaving.

2242
01:24:48,485 --> 01:24:50,018
All you had to do was
say something.

2243
01:24:50,052 --> 01:24:51,520
Gol.

2244
01:24:51,553 --> 01:24:52,988
- [Narrator] Now
there is justice,

2245
01:24:53,022 --> 01:24:55,792
and the clouds over
Julco pass away.

2246
01:24:55,825 --> 01:24:58,193
Out of great sorrow and
spilled blood,

2247
01:24:58,227 --> 01:25:01,230
the forces of good are
sometimes born.

2248
01:25:01,263 --> 01:25:04,800
Hercules and Iole are leaving
now to find a new happiness.

2249
01:25:04,833 --> 01:25:08,303
- [Tom] Six fun-filled
weeks in Jamaica.

2250
01:25:08,337 --> 01:25:09,872
- [Narrator] Where
justice and peace will be

2251
01:25:09,905 --> 01:25:11,842
with them again.

2252
01:25:11,875 --> 01:25:13,543
Farewell Hercules.

2253
01:25:13,577 --> 01:25:14,477
- [Joel] Bye now.

2254
01:25:14,510 --> 01:25:17,347
- [Narrator] Farewell Iole.

2255
01:25:17,380 --> 01:25:21,952
Life awaits you with all its
glory and all its shadows.

2256
01:25:21,985 --> 01:25:23,085
- [Tom] Go forth graduates.

2257
01:25:23,118 --> 01:25:24,887
- [Narrator] But, even through
the most difficult tasks

2258
01:25:24,920 --> 01:25:27,723
the gods may prepare for you.

2259
01:25:27,757 --> 01:25:29,858
- [Crow] Herc and Iole
really had a rocky dating

2260
01:25:29,892 --> 01:25:31,727
and engagement period.

2261
01:25:33,863 --> 01:25:35,965
- [Tom] So, like, ah,
you want to grab a bite,

2262
01:25:35,998 --> 01:25:40,470
or maybe lay out on the
ledo deck or somethin'?

2263
01:25:40,503 --> 01:25:41,770
- [Joel] Or is it?

2264
01:25:41,803 --> 01:25:43,405
- [Tom] I doubt it.

2265
01:25:44,507 --> 01:25:45,975
(siren voicing)

2266
01:25:46,008 --> 01:25:47,743
- [Crow] Valley High.

2267
01:25:50,547 --> 01:25:52,348
What ever happened
to these guys?

2268
01:25:52,382 --> 01:25:54,283
- [Joel] I don't know,
it's kind of inconclusive.

2269
01:25:54,317 --> 01:25:55,652
- [Tom] Oh, I know, you
see, Hercules got a job

2270
01:25:55,685 --> 01:25:56,953
as a prep cook for a while.

2271
01:25:56,987 --> 01:25:58,655
He got fired for tokin'
up on the job.

2272
01:25:58,688 --> 01:26:00,155
He said it was just
because the manager

2273
01:26:00,190 --> 01:26:01,623
didn't like the Greeks.

2274
01:26:01,657 --> 01:26:04,360
And Iole did data entry
at Fingerhut.

2275
01:26:04,393 --> 01:26:05,528
- [Crow] Did they have any kids?

2276
01:26:05,562 --> 01:26:07,897
- [Tom] No, Herc couldn't
perform his husbandly duties,

2277
01:26:07,930 --> 01:26:08,898
if you know what I mean.

2278
01:26:08,932 --> 01:26:09,932
Well, they adopted Ulysses,

2279
01:26:09,965 --> 01:26:11,300
but he became a real
troublesome kid.

2280
01:26:11,333 --> 01:26:13,002
You know, he busted into
a cabin up north

2281
01:26:13,035 --> 01:26:14,437
and took some fishing gear.

2282
01:26:14,470 --> 01:26:16,138
He was on probation for a while.

2283
01:26:16,172 --> 01:26:19,042
I heard he's got connection
to a string of chop shops.

2284
01:26:19,075 --> 01:26:19,908
- [Crow] But Hercules and Iole

2285
01:26:19,942 --> 01:26:21,077
really loved each other, right?

2286
01:26:21,110 --> 01:26:22,345
- [Tom] Well, it depends
on how you define love.

2287
01:26:22,378 --> 01:26:24,047
You know, for Iole, it
got really hard

2288
01:26:24,080 --> 01:26:26,115
to come home from Fingerhut,
night after night,

2289
01:26:26,148 --> 01:26:28,450
see this big demigod
sitting on the couch,

2290
01:26:28,483 --> 01:26:30,720
slamming back Limeys
and watching TV.

2291
01:26:30,753 --> 01:26:32,022
Well, then Herc went
through rehab

2292
01:26:32,055 --> 01:26:33,923
and he started selling
Kirbys door to door.

2293
01:26:33,957 --> 01:26:36,058
Then one day he ran into an
Amazon he knew from the island,

2294
01:26:36,092 --> 01:26:37,193
this Debby.

2295
01:26:37,227 --> 01:26:40,062
Pretty soon Debby was
calling him at home all hours

2296
01:26:40,095 --> 01:26:42,032
and driving past his house
and stuff, all the time.

2297
01:26:42,065 --> 01:26:44,633
Iole just flipped out and then
she left and took Ulysses.

2298
01:26:44,667 --> 01:26:46,402
- [Crow] And Jason,
what about Jason?

2299
01:26:46,435 --> 01:26:47,903
- [Tom] Jason, he sold
the Golden Fleece

2300
01:26:47,937 --> 01:26:49,772
and bought himself a
Rupp Mini Bike.

2301
01:26:49,805 --> 01:26:52,175
His family moved a lot, so
he was in and out of schools,

2302
01:26:52,208 --> 01:26:53,710
never one place for more
than a couple of months.

2303
01:26:53,743 --> 01:26:55,077
Well, he quit school at 15

2304
01:26:55,110 --> 01:26:56,913
and started doing standup
comedy on the road.

2305
01:26:56,947 --> 01:26:58,982
And then one night he
freaked out on stage

2306
01:26:59,015 --> 01:27:01,150
after some guy heckled
him about Madea,

2307
01:27:01,183 --> 01:27:02,952
not to mention that he refused

2308
01:27:02,985 --> 01:27:04,653
to drive a headliner to
Fargo one time.

2309
01:27:04,687 --> 01:27:06,155
So, he didn't get much
work after that.

2310
01:27:06,188 --> 01:27:07,857
Then he was killed in a
tragic boating accident,

2311
01:27:07,890 --> 01:27:08,992
involving the Argo.

2312
01:27:09,025 --> 01:27:11,327
You know, there was some
taunts from cruel crew mates,

2313
01:27:11,360 --> 01:27:12,562
and there was a case of St.
Pauli Girl.

2314
01:27:12,595 --> 01:27:13,428
- [Joel] Are you done?

2315
01:27:13,462 --> 01:27:14,263
- [Tom] No I'm not.

2316
01:27:14,297 --> 01:27:15,498
- [Joel] Yes you are.

2317
01:27:15,532 --> 01:27:17,500
- [Tom] But what about
crayon, you remember crayon?

2318
01:27:17,533 --> 01:27:20,470
He was the one who
went out to the.

2319
01:27:30,212 --> 01:27:31,347
(slamming)

2320
01:27:31,380 --> 01:27:32,582
(shutting)

2321
01:27:32,615 --> 01:27:34,850
(slidding)

2322
01:27:35,818 --> 01:27:37,487
(closing)

2323
01:27:37,520 --> 01:27:38,788
(slamming)

2324
01:27:38,822 --> 01:27:41,123
(shutting)

2325
01:27:41,157 --> 01:27:43,492
- So, Tommy boy, by my
calculations,

2326
01:27:43,525 --> 01:27:46,228
that comes out to be about
15 Amazon women a piece.

2327
01:27:46,262 --> 01:27:47,930
- Yeah, okay, so
it's 15 a piece.

2328
01:27:47,963 --> 01:27:50,165
I admit those are good odds,
but what good would it be?

2329
01:27:50,198 --> 01:27:51,867
Who wants a bunch of
dumb old girls around.

2330
01:27:51,900 --> 01:27:53,035
(sighing)

2331
01:27:53,068 --> 01:27:54,337
I mean, there'd be curling
irons all over the bathrooms

2332
01:27:54,370 --> 01:27:55,738
and hair clogs in the showers,

2333
01:27:55,772 --> 01:27:57,307
not to mention them
wearing our shirts.

2334
01:27:57,340 --> 01:27:59,342
- Tom, are you even
paying attention?

2335
01:27:59,375 --> 01:28:01,543
Seems pretty obvious to me
that if Amazon women were

2336
01:28:01,577 --> 01:28:02,812
to take over the ship,

2337
01:28:02,845 --> 01:28:06,182
you and I would not have
to lift a finger.

2338
01:28:06,215 --> 01:28:07,217
They'll cook, they'll clean,

2339
01:28:07,250 --> 01:28:09,452
they'll empty the load pans.
- Load pans.

2340
01:28:09,485 --> 01:28:12,388
- Squeegee the windows
and peel grapes for us.

2341
01:28:12,422 --> 01:28:13,155
- Wow.

2342
01:28:13,188 --> 01:28:14,257
- And feed them to us.

2343
01:28:14,290 --> 01:28:18,260
They even like to go
horseback riding and swimming.

2344
01:28:18,293 --> 01:28:20,295
- Wow, well, when you
put it that way,

2345
01:28:20,330 --> 01:28:22,365
I guess I could put up
with a few nylons hangin'

2346
01:28:22,398 --> 01:28:24,833
in the bathroom, you know.

2347
01:28:24,867 --> 01:28:29,038
Boy, all our chores
done, snacks on demand,

2348
01:28:29,072 --> 01:28:31,640
lunch every day, kiss bye,

2349
01:28:31,673 --> 01:28:33,175
man, we'd have it made.

2350
01:28:33,208 --> 01:28:34,510
- I know, I know--

2351
01:28:34,543 --> 01:28:36,578
- Okay, okay, listen you guys.

2352
01:28:36,612 --> 01:28:38,580
I've heard every word
you said and I want you

2353
01:28:38,613 --> 01:28:40,617
to know it makes me just sick.

2354
01:28:40,650 --> 01:28:41,617
- What, what?

2355
01:28:41,650 --> 01:28:43,485
Were were just saying
that Amazon women love

2356
01:28:43,518 --> 01:28:44,753
to do stuff for men.

2357
01:28:44,787 --> 01:28:47,490
- Listen, in the first place,
you're not men, you're robots,

2358
01:28:47,523 --> 01:28:48,457
and in the second place,

2359
01:28:48,490 --> 01:28:51,627
not all women carry
curling irons around,

2360
01:28:51,660 --> 01:28:55,330
and in the third place,
you've got Amazons all wrong.

2361
01:28:55,365 --> 01:28:57,033
It's like, they were
noble warriors

2362
01:28:57,067 --> 01:28:58,735
that didn't need men at all.

2363
01:28:58,802 --> 01:29:00,903
It just so happens that
the filmmakers decided

2364
01:29:00,903 --> 01:29:04,507
to take a few liberties
with ancient Greek history

2365
01:29:04,507 --> 01:29:08,410
and add some sexual titillation,
and you rummies bought it.

2366
01:29:08,410 --> 01:29:09,345
(horn honking)

2367
01:29:09,412 --> 01:29:10,547
Oh, we got a ship
coming into range.

2368
01:29:10,613 --> 01:29:12,815
Give me rocket number nine.

2369
01:29:14,817 --> 01:29:16,885
(horn honking)

2370
01:29:16,918 --> 01:29:18,320
Hey, who are you?

2371
01:29:18,353 --> 01:29:20,623
- Oh, hi, I'm Elaine and
this is Carol.

2372
01:29:20,657 --> 01:29:22,058
You know, I must have
taken a wrong turn

2373
01:29:22,092 --> 01:29:23,425
at the Piggly Wiggly.

2374
01:29:23,458 --> 01:29:25,293
You know, we're looking
for the paper drive.

2375
01:29:25,327 --> 01:29:26,962
- [Crow] Well, I can see
by your T-shirt

2376
01:29:26,995 --> 01:29:28,230
that you're an Amazon?

2377
01:29:28,263 --> 01:29:30,900
- Card-carrying since '67.

2378
01:29:30,933 --> 01:29:32,902
- Jeffrey gave us
these T-shirts.

2379
01:29:32,935 --> 01:29:34,603
He's my Cindy's youngest.

2380
01:29:34,637 --> 01:29:36,572
Cute, I am tellin' ya,
that kid, he's got--

2381
01:29:36,605 --> 01:29:37,573
- That's great.

2382
01:29:37,607 --> 01:29:39,208
Could you tell us if
you're gonna conquer us

2383
01:29:39,242 --> 01:29:40,543
or take us over or somethin'?

2384
01:29:40,577 --> 01:29:43,512
- Oh, heavens no, whose
got the time?

2385
01:29:43,545 --> 01:29:45,347
It used to be a full-time thing,

2386
01:29:45,380 --> 01:29:47,883
now we just conquer
men for charity.

2387
01:29:47,917 --> 01:29:49,018
It's real, real fun.

2388
01:29:49,052 --> 01:29:50,185
- Ah, well, in that case,

2389
01:29:50,218 --> 01:29:53,022
maybe you could help my
friends and I get out of space

2390
01:29:53,055 --> 01:29:55,057
and take us back to
Earth or somethin'?

2391
01:29:55,090 --> 01:29:58,160
- Oh no mister, you boys knew
you were gonna be in space,

2392
01:29:58,193 --> 01:29:59,762
you should of arranged a ride.

2393
01:29:59,795 --> 01:30:01,897
I am not mom's taxi.

2394
01:30:01,930 --> 01:30:03,398
- Yah, you kids can walk.

2395
01:30:03,432 --> 01:30:04,667
It's nice out.

2396
01:30:04,700 --> 01:30:05,802
- Well, listen, we gotta run.

2397
01:30:05,835 --> 01:30:07,903
It's nice meetin' you fellas,
buh-bye.

2398
01:30:07,937 --> 01:30:09,272
Nice kids.

2399
01:30:09,305 --> 01:30:11,740
- So, those were Amazons, eh?

2400
01:30:12,942 --> 01:30:14,777
Nice, but not at all
what I expected.

2401
01:30:14,810 --> 01:30:15,978
- No, not at all.

2402
01:30:16,012 --> 01:30:17,113
- Yeah, me neither.

2403
01:30:17,147 --> 01:30:20,783
Geez, they seemed like
somebody's moms or something.

2404
01:30:20,817 --> 01:30:23,953
She said they were semi-retired,

2405
01:30:23,987 --> 01:30:27,257
but still I imagine an
Amazon being a noble warrior

2406
01:30:27,290 --> 01:30:29,358
with one cut off and--

2407
01:30:29,392 --> 01:30:30,827
(throat clearing)

2408
01:30:30,860 --> 01:30:32,962
Listen, let's just, ah,
I'm not feeling very good.

2409
01:30:32,995 --> 01:30:34,263
Let's hurry up with the mads,

2410
01:30:34,297 --> 01:30:36,832
and I'm gonna lay down, you can
make me a soup and sandwich.

2411
01:30:36,865 --> 01:30:37,667
- Okay.

2412
01:30:37,700 --> 01:30:39,735
- Come in sirs, please.

2413
01:30:39,768 --> 01:30:41,737
- Oh, Frank, bring me that memo.

2414
01:30:41,770 --> 01:30:43,705
Oh, Frank, bring me some coffee.

2415
01:30:43,738 --> 01:30:46,275
Yes, I'm Dr. Forester, I'm
king of the whole world.

2416
01:30:46,308 --> 01:30:47,343
(groaning)

2417
01:30:47,377 --> 01:30:50,212
(laughing) Sorry, I
didn't mean to.

2418
01:30:50,245 --> 01:30:51,880
I was just about to.

2419
01:30:51,913 --> 01:30:53,348
- Push the button perhaps?

2420
01:30:53,382 --> 01:30:55,217
- You know me so well.

2421
01:30:59,555 --> 01:31:02,492
(electronic music)

2422
01:32:03,418 --> 01:32:05,822
- He's something out
of a bad dream.

